# Conventional Commits: <type>: <summary>
# Optional scope: <type>(<scope>): <summary>
#
# Types:
# feat:     a new feature for the user
# fix:      a bug fix for the user
# docs:     documentation only
# refactor: a code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# perf:     a code change that improves performance
# test:     adding or correcting tests
# build:    the build system or external dependencies
# ci:       continuous integration configuration and scripts
# chore:    other changes that touch neither source nor tests
# style:    formatting that does not change meaning
# revert:   reverts a previous commit
#
# Optionally add a body after a blank line to explain the change.
# Put footers after another blank line.
#
# For a breaking change, put ! immediately before the colon and describe
# the breaking change in the summary, or add this footer:
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description of the breaking change>
#
# Specification: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
